[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2651331767","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/102717#issuecomment-2651331767","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102717","id":2651331767,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6eCBy3","user":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-11T16:25:31Z","updated_at":"2025-02-11T16:25:31Z","body":"> This PR removes any mention of specific scene nodes in the various error/warning messages found in `modules/jolt_physics`, due to calls to `Node::to_string` being problematic when using `physics/3d/run_on_separate_thread`.\r\n\r\nI missed that the linked issue was only when running physics on a separate thread (which isn't the default). In that case maybe it still makes sense to preserve the detailed messages for the case where `physics/3d/run_on_separate_thread` is `false`, and only fall back to a more generic message in the other case?","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2651331767/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2651433934","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/102717#issuecomment-2651433934","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102717","id":2651433934,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6eCavO","user":{"login":"mihe","id":4884246,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4ODQyNDY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4884246?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe","html_url":"https://github.com/mihe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-11T16:50:44Z","updated_at":"2025-02-11T16:50:44Z","body":"> In that case maybe it still makes sense to preserve the detailed messages for the case where `physics/3d/run_on_separate_thread` is `false`, and only fall back to a more generic message in the other case?\r\n\r\nHaving two different error message everywhere would be quite messy. I could however make it so that any node name is reported as `<unknown>` or something when running on a separate thread, which wouldn't require changing the existing messages in any way. I already [do this](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/5da6deaaca27f3d4ec5281d5b791408570919f15/modules/jolt_physics/objects/jolt_object_3d.cpp#L141) if the instance ID (`ObjectID` in the case of nodes) isn't found in `ObjectDB`.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2651433934/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2651458863","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/102717#issuecomment-2651458863","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102717","id":2651458863,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6eCg0v","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-11T16:57:11Z","updated_at":"2025-02-11T16:57:17Z","body":">  I could however make it so that any node name is reported as `<unknown>` or something when running on a separate thread, which wouldn't require changing the existing messages in any way.\r\n\r\nThat makes sense to me, as long as we document this limitation in `run_in_separate_thread`'s documen